[&ldquo;And where is the lamb for the offering?&rdquo;]

(see there well).

And all this is the aspect of Rosh HaShanah. For Rosh HaShanah is the first day of the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah, and the main t&rsquo;shuvah is through what is explained in the aforementioned Torah &mdash; through seeking, requesting, searching, crying out, and asking: &ldquo;Ayeh &mdash; Where is the place of His kavod?&rdquo; (as is explained in its place, in the aforementioned siman). For anyone can understand that for most people who are not mighty warriors as they should be, it is very difficult for them to return in t&rsquo;shuvah. For since their yaitzer has already overpowered them and they did not overpower it to subdue it &mdash; since they are already ensnared, it is certainly difficult for them to return in t&rsquo;shuvah. Especially those who have descended and fallen greatly, until their heart is in the aspect of s&rsquo;charchor [spinning/dizziness] explained there &mdash; that the k&rsquo;lipah that has clung to them through their sins twists and turns the heart with many distortions, confusions, and bewilderments. And as he said then explicitly in Yiddish: &ldquo;It twists the heart around.&rdquo;

It emerges that the horn of the Shofar came into being through the aspect of &ldquo;And where is the lamb for the offering?&rdquo; Therefore we blow the Shofar on Rosh HaShanah, for then is the beginning of t&rsquo;shuvah, whose main essence is through the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; &mdash; which is the aspect of the Shofar. For because the Shofar is drawn from there, its kol has the power to awaken every person to take to heart and remember his eternal purpose &mdash; and in the final end, what will become of him. And even if it is still difficult for him to return in t&rsquo;shuvah, at least he should walk in the aforementioned path: to spend his days seeking Hashem, to ask each day constantly, &ldquo;Where is the place of His kavod?&rdquo; For this is the main t&rsquo;shuvah. And as is written: &ldquo;And you will seek from there Hashem your G-d, and you will find&rdquo; (D&rsquo;varim 4:29) &mdash; &ldquo;from there&rdquo; specifically. And as is brought in the name of the Baal Shem Tov, of blessed memory: &ldquo;And you will seek from there&rdquo; &mdash; &ldquo;from there&rdquo; specifically &mdash; from whatever place one has descended and fallen to, even to the filthy places &mdash; &ldquo;from there&rdquo; specifically, one needs to seek with all his heart and with all his soul for Hashem, blessed be He, in the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo;

And all this is the aspect of Rosh HaShanah, which is a hidden, concealed, and very secret matter, the aspect of the beginning of Creation, which is the secret of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; &mdash; which is a sealed utterance [ma&rsquo;amar sasum], the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; as is explained in the aforementioned Torah. And therefore we say then: &ldquo;Before You all hidden things are revealed, and the multitude of secrets from the beginning,&rdquo; &ldquo;for this day is the beginning of Your works.&rdquo; For all of Creation &mdash; especially the creation of Adam, who was created on this day and includes all of Creation &mdash; its essence was through the aspect of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; which includes all the ten utterances (as is explained there). And this is the aspect of &ldquo;Blow the Shofar at the chodesh, at the keseh&rdquo; &mdash; &ldquo;ba&rsquo;keseh&rdquo; specifically &mdash; a language of sealed and concealed, the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; which is the aspect of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, which is sealed and concealed and very hidden. And from there is the main tikkun of t&rsquo;shuvah.

And therefore one needs to travel to true Tzaddikim for Rosh HaShanah. And even one who does not merit to travel, at least he should try to go to a place where there is a large gathering of upright and G-d-fearing people, to pray and hear the kol Shofar with them &mdash; as is the custom of all Yisrael, that on Rosh HaShanah and Yom Kippur they gather together from all the villages. And all those far away who are not careful to pray with the tzibbur throughout the year &mdash; on Rosh HaShanah they all gather to the holy congregation. For the main aspect of introducing this path of t&rsquo;shuvah through the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; &mdash; no one knows except the great true Tzaddikim. For every true Tzaddik is the aspect of Moshiach &mdash; he knows the secret of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, upon which Rebbe Shimon bar Yochai revealed seventy facets, which they customarily study during these days, in Elul and the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah &mdash; which is the holy Sefer Ha&rsquo;Tikkunim.

And this is: &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis bara Elokim &hellip; and the earth was tohu va&rsquo;vohu, and darkness upon the face of the deep&rdquo; &mdash; which are the aspect of the totality of the four exiles, as our Sages said &mdash; which are the totality of the Sitra Achara and the k&rsquo;lipos, whose sustenance comes from the concealment of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance. But: &ldquo;And the spirit of G-d&rdquo; &mdash; this is the spirit of Moshiach &mdash; &ldquo;hovered over the face of the waters.&rdquo; For the main tikkun is through him &mdash; through introducing the path of Hashem into the world, to seek and search &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo; Through this the descent is transformed into ascent, and one ascends to the holiness of the sealed utterance, &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis.&rdquo; And this is &ldquo;upon the face of the waters&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;Pour out your heart like water&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of t&rsquo;shuvah accomplished through this.

And this is the aspect of Rosh HaShanah, the aspect of kol Shofar, which is the aspect of &ldquo;From the depths I called to You, Hashem.&rdquo; For the main intention of the Shofar is that the kol should ascend higher and higher, until we merit to arouse the great mercy &mdash; the abundant mercy hidden in the sealed utterance, in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis.&rdquo; For from its extreme concealment, the severe dinim draw sustenance &mdash; from which comes the sustenance of all the chitzonim and all the filthy places. And it is impossible to sweeten these severe dinim except at their root &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis.&rdquo;

And for this purpose comes the holy kol Shofar, which is a very strong and mighty kol, in the aspect of &ldquo;The kol Shofar was very strong,&rdquo; and in the aspect of &ldquo;And the kol of the Shofar went and grew ever stronger&rdquo; &mdash; ascending to the sealed utterance and revealing from there His G-dliness and His might and His dominion and His Kingship, which rules over all. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;Elokim has ascended with a T&rsquo;ruah&rdquo; &mdash; which at first glance is not understood in its simple meaning: how can &ldquo;ascent&rdquo; apply to Hashem? But the intention simply is that the Torah speaks in the language of human beings: since through the Shofar His G-dliness and Kingship are revealed, it is considered, as it were, an ascent. But according to what was explained above, the matter is clearer. For &ldquo;Elokim&rdquo; is the aspect of dinim, and from there descend the dross of the dinim from which the Sitra Achara draws sustenance. But their entire root is from &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance. And through the kol of the T&rsquo;ruah of Yisrael, the kol ascends there and reveals the concealment &mdash; through which all the dinim and chitzonim who draw sustenance from there are nullified. Then is fulfilled: &ldquo;Elokim has ascended with a T&rsquo;ruah&rdquo; &mdash; &ldquo;Elokim&rdquo; specifically, the aspect of dinim, ascends through the T&rsquo;ruah to its supreme root, the aspect of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis.&rdquo; For the kol Shofar reaches there. This is the sweetening of the dinim at their root.

And similarly in the mizmor &ldquo;Elokim Y&rsquo;chanainu&rdquo; that we say then in the morning &mdash; as is written: &ldquo;To make known upon the earth Your way, among all nations Your salvation. The peoples will thank You, Elokim &hellip; the peoples will thank You, all of them.&rdquo; And similarly at the entrance of Shabbos, &ldquo;L&rsquo;chu N&rsquo;ran&rsquo;nah&rdquo; &mdash; which speaks much of this, that His G-dliness should be revealed among all the peoples. And similarly in this mizmor that we say on Rosh HaShanah before the Shofar: &ldquo;All the nations, clap hands &hellip; For Hashem Most High is awesome &hellip; He is a great King over all the earth &hellip; He will subdue peoples beneath us, and nations.&rdquo; For through revealing the sealed utterance, all the nations are subdued and fall and are nullified to holiness.

And therefore all year we say &ldquo;HaKeil HaKadosh,&rdquo; and on Rosh HaShanah &ldquo;HaMelech HaKadosh.&rdquo; For even though the Name Keil is holier &mdash; it is one of the seven Names that may not be erased, while &ldquo;Melech&rdquo; is an appellation that may be erased &mdash; even so, on Rosh HaShanah we mention &ldquo;Melech&rdquo; specifically, to indicate that now His Kingship is revealed from the aspect of &ldquo;Kadosh&rdquo; specifically, which is the aspect of sealed and hidden. For &ldquo;kadosh&rdquo; is a language of separation and distinction.

For throughout the year one cannot begin except from the aspect of &ldquo;Keil&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of chesed, the first attribute of the seven days of building, the aspect of &ldquo;The world is built through chesed&rdquo; &mdash; from there is the main beginning of the revealed utterances. But now, the end of deed ascends to the beginning of thought &mdash; the aspect of Malchus, which is the last attribute, which in our many sins, especially in our exile, is in the aspect of &ldquo;she descended wondrously, for her feet descend to death&rdquo; &mdash; until she became hidden in the bad places. But on Rosh HaShanah and the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah, which is the beginning of t&rsquo;shuvah through the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; &mdash; through this His Kingship is revealed from &ldquo;Kadosh&rdquo; specifically, from the sealed utterance, which we work to reveal through the t&rsquo;shuvah, the seeking and searching &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;Let us search our ways and investigate, and let us return to Hashem.&rdquo;

But when a person sins, chas v&rsquo;shalom &mdash; especially when the sins of the generation multiply until they cause the exile or its lengthening &mdash; then all the holinesses ascend upward. And then the Malchus is in the secret of a point, and she descends wondrously. And the main aspect remaining in her is the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo; And one who merits to have compassion upon himself and to search &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; &mdash; then his descent is the purpose of his ascent, and he ascends to the root of Malchus, which is Keser Elyon, the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; the aspect of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance. And through this specifically is his tikkun. And all this is done mainly on Rosh HaShanah and the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah.

And then, through the t&rsquo;shuvah &mdash; that the totality of Yisrael are awakened and come in humility before Hashem and request that He return us in complete t&rsquo;shuvah &mdash; through this they ascend to the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; the root of everything, in the aspect of &ldquo;Return, Yisrael, to Hashem your G-d, for you have stumbled through your iniquity&rdquo; &mdash; so much so that you have no remedy except to return to Hashem your G-d Himself. For the good point [n&rsquo;kudah tovah] hiding in the heart of even the worst of the worst knows in general that there is a G-d who rules and governs, and to Him alone we have sinned, and with Him is the forgiveness, as is written: &ldquo;To You alone I have sinned,&rdquo; and: &ldquo;For with You is the forgiveness.&rdquo;

And this is the aspect of &ldquo;Great is t&rsquo;shuvah, for it reaches the Throne of Glory&rdquo; &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; which is the root of the Throne of Glory, the aspect of Kisei d&rsquo;mis&rsquo;kasya l&rsquo;aila. And therefore we say then &ldquo;HaMelech HaKadosh.&rdquo; For the main name &ldquo;Kadosh&rdquo; is said regarding Keser, the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; which is entirely holy, entirely good, including all the ten holinesses. And from there specifically we now draw His Kingship upon us through the t&rsquo;shuvah, the seeking and searching &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo; And there is much to explain according to the ways of the wisdom of truth, the holy Kabbalah. But all our engagement is only to explain what emerges from the words of Rabbainu according to the aforementioned Torah &mdash; what is relevant to the arousal of t&rsquo;shuvah in truth, so that even the worst of the worst should merit to find counsel and strategy, a way and path and trail, to return to Hashem from wherever he is. And the main thing is through the seeking and searching &ldquo;Ayeh,&rdquo; mentioned above.

For in truth, everything is from Him, as is written: &ldquo;Who has given Me anything beforehand, that I should repay him?&rdquo; And: &ldquo;For all is from You, and from Your hand we have given to You.&rdquo; But even so, one needs at least some is&rsquo;arusa dil&rsquo;sata [arousal from below]. For all the worlds without number that depend on this world, on this person &mdash; everything was created only for this. And the totality of the arousal from below is the aspect of tz&rsquo;dakah &mdash; the aspect of action, of hands, the aspect of &ldquo;You shall surely open your hand to him.&rdquo; And the main tz&rsquo;dakah is when one merits to give to the one from whom one receives &mdash; who boasted that he is the main ba&rsquo;al tz&rsquo;dakah, that whoever receives, he gives to him &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;More than the householder does for the poor person, the poor person does for the householder.&rdquo;

But one needs to beseech Hashem greatly and to give much tz&rsquo;dakah for the sake of Heaven, until one merits to find a worthy poor person. As our Sages said: &ldquo;Lest you think anyone who wants to leap can leap &mdash; the Torah teaches: &lsquo;How precious is Your kindness, Elokim.&rsquo;&rdquo; For there are many who cause more damage through their tz&rsquo;dakah (as is explained in siman 15). And also all the deeds and good works are all called tz&rsquo;dakah, as is written: &ldquo;And it will be tz&rsquo;dakah for us, that we observe to do.&rdquo; But the beginning of all beginnings is from the mitzvah of actual tz&rsquo;dakah. And as is the custom of all Yisrael, that before prayer one gives tz&rsquo;dakah. And especially before Rosh HaShanah and the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah, one gives much tz&rsquo;dakah &mdash; for tz&rsquo;dakah to a worthy poor person who is included in the aforementioned ba&rsquo;al ko&rsquo;ach &mdash; from there is the main beginning.

And also one who is a great pauper and has no money to give tz&rsquo;dakah &mdash; even so, he too needs to give some small thing, whatever is possible, to a worthy poor person, as our Sages said: that even a poor person should give tz&rsquo;dakah. For the offering of the poor person is very precious. And the main thing is that what one endures toil, exertion, shedding of blood, and humiliations to draw close to the truth &mdash; this is the main tz&rsquo;dakah, the aspect of arousal from below. For in truth, the Tzaddik does not need the world at all for himself; on the contrary, from him come all the influences and all the wealth in the world, as our Sages said: &ldquo;The whole world is sustained on account of Chanina My son, and Chanina My son has enough with a kav of carobs.&rdquo; Rather, one needs to give him tz&rsquo;dakah for our sake, for our own tikkun.

And all the healing through the t&rsquo;shuvah is only through the aforementioned path, the aspect of &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, in which everything is included. For all the ten utterances are included in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; (as is understood there). For all the aspects mentioned there are ten by ten: ten types of arrows to be extracted, ten walls of water through the tz&rsquo;dakah of the ba&rsquo;al ko&rsquo;ach, ten types of pulses, and ten types of melody. And all are included in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, from which come all the ten utterances. But there, in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; everything is sealed and very hidden &mdash; and from the magnitude of its concealment, all the chitzonim draw sustenance from there, from which come all the ten types of arrows shot at the Bas Melech, K&rsquo;nesses Yisrael.

And the main healing is through having such power in his hands that he could extract all the arrows &mdash; and his main power comes from &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance itself. For from there is their sustenance and from there is their subjugation &mdash; through introducing into the souls of Yisrael to seek and search &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo; And this is what is written in the story: that he boasted that he has such power that even when he shoots an arrow, he can bring it back. And at first glance it is difficult: why does he need to shoot it and then bring it back? Would it not be better not to shoot it at all? But it is the secret of the sealed utterance, from which the chitzonim draw sustenance &mdash; and this is a great necessity for the sustaining of the world, which is sustained through the fact that there is specifically free choice. Therefore he boasted that he shoots an arrow and brings it back &mdash; for from the sealed utterance come all the arrows, the forces of the Sitra Achara, and from there specifically their subjugation, through seeking and searching &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo;

And this is &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; &mdash; which alludes to t&rsquo;shuvah, as is written in Tikunay Zohar: &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; [rearranged] spells yarai boshes [one who fears shame] &mdash; the aspect of t&rsquo;shuvah, whose main essence is through bushah [shame], as is explained (in siman 72, Likutay Tinyana). Also, the letters of boshes rearrange to spell tashev [you will return] &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;You turn man back to dust and say, &lsquo;Return, children of man&rsquo;&rdquo; &mdash; which is the aforementioned aspect: that even if a person has fallen to the filthy places, the aspect of the crushing of the soul [dich&rsquo;duchah shel nefesh] &mdash; even then one needs to search and seek until he returns to Hashem, in the aspect of &ldquo;You turn man back to dust&rdquo; &mdash; which our Sages expound: &ldquo;until the crushing of the soul.&rdquo; Even then: &ldquo;And You say: Return.&rdquo;

All of this is the aspect of healing the Bas Melech who fled into the ten walls of water, into whom all the ten types of arrows were shot. For the libations are brought at the time of the offerings &mdash; and all the offerings are for clarifying the sparks and souls from the deepest depths of the k&rsquo;lipos. And then one brings libations and pours them in the Bais HaMikdash into the shisin that descend to the abyss, to raise the most deeply fallen souls (as is explained in Choshen Mishpat, Hilchos G&rsquo;viyas Chov, Halacha 5). And therefore the shisin are alluded to in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; for the main tikkun of these souls that descended to the abyss is through &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, through seeking and searching &ldquo;Ayeh.&rdquo;

And therefore we say a shir [song] at the time of the libations &mdash; for the main healing of the Bas Melech is through song and melody, the aspect of the ten types of melody (as is explained in the story) &mdash; that the waves of the sea, which are the aspect of the ten walls, are formed by the winds, from which come the ten types of melody (see there well). For the entire story, in which very lofty Toros are hidden, is all connected &mdash; everything told there in groups of ten is all tied and joined together.

It emerges that &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; alludes to the ten walls of water. It is also explained in Rashi&rsquo;s commentary on &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis&rdquo; that the waters preceded the world and their creation is not mentioned explicitly in the Torah &mdash; and all things were created from the water. And all this is the above matter: the waters that preceded the world were created through &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance. And because this utterance is so sealed and hidden, the waters &mdash; the totality of Creation &mdash; are sealed and hidden in the account of creation. For their creation is hidden in &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis.&rdquo;

Raishay P&rsquo;rakim &mdash; 3

And this is the aspect of why we begin to say Bircas Geshem on Sh&rsquo;mini Atzeres &mdash; &ldquo;Mashiv ha&rsquo;ru&rsquo;ach u&rsquo;morid ha&rsquo;gashem.&rdquo; For all the rains of blessing are drawn through the clouds, whose entire power to hold the water and bring it down in proper time and measure &mdash; so they should not flood the world, but rather bring blessing and abundance &mdash; all this is through the ten walls of water. And these ten walls are maintained by the ru&rsquo;ach [wind/spirit], which is the aspect of simchah. And therefore we say &ldquo;Mashiv ha&rsquo;ru&rsquo;ach u&rsquo;morid ha&rsquo;gashem&rdquo; &mdash; for the rains drawn from the ten walls come through the wind that upholds them. And we begin on Sh&rsquo;mini Atzeres, when the main intensity of the simchah is, the aspect of &ldquo;And you shall be only joyful.&rdquo;

And this is the aspect of the ten types of melody drawn through the ba&rsquo;al ko&rsquo;ach who knows how to create a balance for all ten types of winds that maintain the ten walls of water, from which come all the rains. And this is: &ldquo;Hashem will open for you His good treasury, to give rain to your land in its time.&rdquo; For the rain is drawn from the good treasury &mdash; the aspect of the wondrous chambers of the fortress of water that has the ten walls.

And this is the aspect of the four species, whose mitzvah is specifically in the hands, as is written: &ldquo;And you shall take for yourselves on the first day&rdquo; &mdash; to draw upon us the power of the hands. For through the wavings we extract the arrows.

For the four species correspond to the four aspects: the lulav corresponds to extracting the arrows. Arvay nachal correspond to the water. Hadas is the aspect of the vitality of the n&rsquo;shamah, the aspect of wisdom &mdash; through which one knows the pulse, how to revive the souls included in the Bas Melech, the aspect of &ldquo;Sustain me with raisin cakes.&rdquo; Esrog is the aspect of the main simchah that revives the Bas Melech, who is the aspect of the esrog, the aspect of &ldquo;You are entirely beautiful, my beloved.&rdquo;

And through this we merit to finish the Torah and to &ldquo;all the mighty hand,&rdquo; and to return and begin &ldquo;B&rsquo;raishis,&rdquo; the sealed utterance, to which we need each year to return and ascend, to draw Torah from there. And this is the aspect of Yom Kippur, the completion of the Ten Days of T&rsquo;shuvah, when the Second Tablets were given in private &mdash; in which we engage all year through the t&rsquo;shuvah. And on each day of the Ten Days, they worked to build the Malchus, one attribute each day, through the power of the t&rsquo;shuvah of Rosh HaShanah &mdash; and the completion on Yom Kippur, which is the aspect of Keser Malchus, upon which is said &ldquo;He tells from the beginning the end.&rdquo; And then one draws Torah from there &mdash; through which one returns and reveals from the aspect of &ldquo;Ayeh&rdquo; specifically that the fullness of the earth is His kavod. And all this needs much explanation.
